# =============================================================================
# BIRANCHI KULESIKA — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION (.env.example)
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# By default, local development uses DATA_SOURCE=mock which requires NO external
# database or API keys. Everything runs in-memory with instant reset capabilities.
#
# Follow the detailed documentation below for each variable.
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 1. CORE APPLICATION & DATA SOURCE
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA_SOURCE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: DATA_SOURCE
# 2. What it is: Primary switch controlling the data persistence adapter.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Toggles between the in-memory mock repository
#    (zero-dependency development) and the live Supabase PostgreSQL repository.
# 4. Where to get it: Set manually to mock for local dev or supabase for live DB.
# 5. Expected format: String literal: mock or supabase.
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/config/env.ts -> getDataSource()
#    - lib/repositories/index.ts -> getContentRepository()
# 7. Server/client: Server-only.
# 8. Security implications: Non-secret configuration flag. Any value other than
#    mock or supabase triggers a loud application crash to prevent silent fallbacks.
# 9. Common mistakes: Setting to postgres or production (unsupported values).
# 10. Troubleshooting: If the app throws an invalid data source error, verify
#     that DATA_SOURCE is set to exactly mock or supabase.
# 11. Required: Yes (Defaults to mock if unset).
# 12. Environment behavior: Use mock locally; use supabase in production.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA_SOURCE=mock


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
# 2. What it is: The canonical public base URL of the website.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Required for generating canonical SEO tags, sitemap.xml,
#    robots.txt, dynamic Open Graph images, JSON-LD structured schemas, and OAuth callbacks.
# 4. Where to get it: Set to http://localhost:3000 locally, or your production domain.
# 5. Expected format: Full URL without trailing slash (e.g., http://localhost:3000).
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/constants.ts -> SITE_URL
#    - lib/seo.ts -> rootMetadata, postMetadata, noteMetadata, websiteJsonLd
#    - app/sitemap.ts -> dynamic sitemap entries
#    - app/robots.ts -> sitemap link
#    - app/admin/login/actions.ts -> OAuth redirect URL
# 7. Server/client: Client-safe (prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_).
# 8. Security implications: Public value. Ensure production uses HTTPS to prevent
#    insecure canonical URLs or OAuth redirect mismatches.
# 9. Common mistakes: Adding a trailing slash (e.g., http://localhost:3000/), which
#    causes double slashes in generated canonical URLs.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If Open Graph images or sitemaps show incorrect domains,
#     verify that NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL matches your active hostname.
# 11. Required: Yes (Defaults to http://localhost:3000 if unset).
# 12. Environment behavior: http://localhost:3000 in dev; https://biranchikulesika.com in prod.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000


# =============================================================================
# 2. SUPABASE (POSTGRESQL DATABASE & STORAGE)
# =============================================================================
# Required only when DATA_SOURCE=supabase.
# When DATA_SOURCE=mock, these variables are not required.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
# 2. What it is: The HTTPS endpoint URL of your Supabase project.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Used to initialize Supabase clients for querying tables,
#    authenticating sessions, and accessing public storage assets.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Supabase Dashboard (https://supabase.com/dashboard)
#    → Select your project
#    → Project Settings (Gear icon in sidebar)
#    → API
#    → Project URL
# 5. Expected format: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/supabase/server.ts -> getSupabaseAdmin(), getSupabasePublic(), getSupabaseServer()
#    - app/admin/login/actions.ts
#    - app/admin/auth/callback/route.ts
# 7. Server/client: Client-safe (prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_).
# 8. Security implications: Public endpoint. Protected by Row-Level Security (RLS) policies.
# 9. Common mistakes: Copying the database connection string instead of the API project URL.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If database connection fails with network errors, verify the project
#     URL is active and not paused in the Supabase dashboard.
# 11. Required: Conditional (Required if DATA_SOURCE=supabase).
# 12. Environment behavior: Same project URL across dev/prod if sharing database, or separate
#     staging project URL.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# 2. What it is: The Supabase anonymous/publishable API key.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Used for browser and server client operations that respect
#    Row-Level Security (RLS) policies (public content reads and user auth sessions).
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Supabase Dashboard
#    → Project Settings
#    → API
#    → Project API keys
#    → anon / public
# 5. Expected format: Long JWT string starting with eyJhbGciOi... or modern sb_pub_...
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/supabase/server.ts -> getSupabasePublic(), getSupabaseServer()
#    - app/admin/login/actions.ts
#    - app/admin/auth/callback/route.ts
# 7. Server/client: Client-safe (prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_).
# 8. Security implications: Safe to expose to browsers. RLS policies restrict what data
#    this key can access.
# 9. Common mistakes: Accidentally pasting the service_role secret key here.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If public reads fail with 401 Unauthorized, verify that the key
#     has not expired and belongs to the correct project.
# 11. Required: Conditional (Required if DATA_SOURCE=supabase).
# 12. Environment behavior: Matches the Supabase project configured in NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY
# 2. What it is: The Supabase service-role administrative API secret key.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Used by the repository layer (SupabaseContentRepository)
#    to perform administrative CRUD operations, bypassing RLS on trusted server contexts.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Supabase Dashboard
#    → Project Settings
#    → API
#    → Project API keys
#    → service_role (Secret)
# 5. Expected format: Long JWT string starting with eyJhbGciOi... or modern sb_secret_...
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/supabase/server.ts -> getSupabaseAdmin()
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (CRITICAL SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: CRITICAL. This key bypasses all Row-Level Security policies.
#    NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never commit to Git, never import into client components.
#    If leaked, rotate immediately in the Supabase dashboard.
# 9. Common mistakes: Renaming to NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY or leaking into client code.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If server actions throw "Missing Supabase configuration", verify
#     SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY is present in your server environment variables.
# 11. Required: Conditional (Required if DATA_SOURCE=supabase).
# 12. Environment behavior: Server-only across all environments.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...


# =============================================================================
# 3. RAZORPAY (PATRONAGE & SUPPORT PAYMENTS)
# =============================================================================
# Optional for local development. If unset, the support page uses an instant
# simulated payment confirmation flow with receipt generation.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID
# 2. What it is: The public Razorpay Key ID for client-side checkout modal.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Initializes the Razorpay Checkout SDK popup on /support.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Razorpay Dashboard (https://dashboard.razorpay.com)
#    → Settings / Account & Settings
#    → API Keys
#    → Generate / View Key ID
# 5. Expected format: rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx (Test) or rzp_live_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx (Live).
# 6. Used by:
#    - components/support-page.tsx -> RazorpayConstructor options
# 7. Server/client: Client-safe (prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_).
# 8. Security implications: Public identifier. Cannot be used to capture funds or refund
#    without the secret key.
# 9. Common mistakes: Pasting the Secret Key instead of Key ID.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If Razorpay modal displays "Invalid Key ID", verify key matches
#     your active mode (Test vs Live) in the Razorpay dashboard.
# 11. Required: Optional (Falls back to simulated patronage in local mock mode).
# 12. Environment behavior: Use rzp_test_... for staging/dev; rzp_live_... in production.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_...


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET
# 2. What it is: The private Razorpay API secret key for HMAC signature verification.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Cryptographically verifies payment signatures
#    (HMAC-SHA256 of order_id + payment_id) when confirming patronage.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Razorpay Dashboard
#    → Settings
#    → API Keys
#    → Key Secret
# 5. Expected format: 24+ character alphanumeric secret string.
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/razorpay.ts -> verifyPaymentSignature()
#    - lib/services/content.service.ts -> confirmPayment()
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: Secret. Allows API access to your Razorpay account.
#    Keep strictly server-side.
# 9. Common mistakes: Exposing in client-side code or mixing up Test and Live keys.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If payment confirmation fails with "Invalid payment signature",
#     ensure RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET matches the exact Key ID used on the client.
# 11. Required: Optional (Required if verifying Razorpay order checkout signatures).
# 12. Environment behavior: Test secret locally; Live secret in production.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=...


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# 2. What it is: Secret token used to verify Razorpay webhook payloads.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Validates the X-Razorpay-Signature HTTP header on POST requests
#    to /api/webhooks/razorpay to prevent spoofed payment captured events.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Razorpay Dashboard
#    → Settings
#    → Webhooks
#    → Add New Webhook (URL: https://your-domain.com/api/webhooks/razorpay)
#    → Enter Secret field
# 5. Expected format: Custom secret string chosen during webhook setup.
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/razorpay.ts -> verifyWebhookSignature()
#    - lib/services/content.service.ts -> processRazorpayWebhook()
#    - app/api/webhooks/razorpay/route.ts
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: Secret. If leaked, an attacker could forge payment webhook events.
# 9. Common mistakes: Putting the API Key Secret instead of the Webhook Secret.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If webhooks return 400 "Invalid webhook signature", verify the secret
#     in Razorpay Webhook settings matches this environment variable.
# 11. Required: Optional (Required if receiving live Razorpay webhooks).
# 12. Environment behavior: Set in production and local webhook tunnels (e.g. ngrok).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...


# =============================================================================
# 4. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES & INTEGRATIONS (OPTIONAL)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PEXELS_API_KEY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: PEXELS_API_KEY
# 2. What it is: API key for Pexels photo search.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Fetches daily rotating high-resolution atmosphere wallpapers
#    for the admin login screen (/admin/login).
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Pexels API Portal (https://www.pexels.com/api/)
#    → Create free account / Sign in
#    → Your API Key
# 5. Expected format: 56-character alphanumeric string.
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/services/pexels.service.ts -> fetchFromPexels()
#    - app/api/login-background/route.ts
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: Secret API key. Low blast radius (free tier image lookup).
# 9. Common mistakes: Forgetting to set header Authorization: <key>.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If background image fails to load, verify API key quota and network access.
# 11. Required: Optional (Falls back to curated local dark wallpapers if unset).
# 12. Environment behavior: Safe to use same key across dev and prod.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PEXELS_API_KEY=...


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY / GROQ_API_KEY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: OPENAI_API_KEY or GROQ_API_KEY
# 2. What it is: LLM provider API key for editorial metadata generation.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Automatically generates suggested tags, persona classification,
#    and SEO descriptions in the MDX Composer (/admin/compose).
# 4. Where to get it:
#    OpenAI: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#    Groq: https://console.groq.com/keys
# 5. Expected format: sk-proj-... (OpenAI) or gsk_... (Groq).
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/services/ai-metadata.service.ts -> generateDocumentAiMetadata()
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: Secret API key. Rate limited on the server.
# 9. Common mistakes: Exposing in client bundles.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If AI suggestion button fails in composer, the system falls
#     back seamlessly to deterministic local heuristic NLP.
# 11. Required: Optional (Falls back to local NLP heuristic generator if unset).
# 12. Environment behavior: Optional across all environments.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
